go_test: build external test packages (package <name>_test).

Upstream go_test fails on a source that declares package <name>_test
("External tests are not supported"). go test compiles those files as a
package of their own, <import path>_test, which imports the package as
built with its internal tests, and the generated test main imports both.
go_test now does the same:

- pkg_analyzer reports XTestImports and XTestEmbedPatterns next to the
  internal tests' imports and embeds, and go_list.bzl parses them.
- The internal test package leaves the external test files out instead of
  failing on them. A GoBuildConfig with x_test builds the external ones
  instead (go_list_for_x_test), reusing the internal build's go list
  (declare_package_build's new go_list_out). Its argsfile lists the
  external test files.
- go_test builds that package after the internal one, with the internal
  one in its pkgs, and links it in. Without external test files it is
  empty, and nothing imports it.
- testmaingen takes the external test files with --xtest-files and imports
  their package as _xtest, as cmd/go/internal/load/test.go does; the test
  lister (TPX_LIST_TESTS_COMMAND) reads them too.
- A test files argsfile with no files is empty instead of a blank line,
  which the generator and the lister would read as a file name.
- The external tests may import a package that imports the package under
  test, directly or not (a testutil package, say). go test builds every
  such package again for the test binary, against the package with its
  internal tests (recompileForTest), so the binary holds one copy of it.
  go_test does the same: go_library provides how it builds its package
  (GoPkgBuild, in a GoPkgBuildInfo tset over its deps), and go_test builds
  each such package again from it, deps first, under its own
  recompiled_for_test/<import path> (declare_package_build's new
  output_prefix). The external test package compiles against these, and
  link's new replaced_pkgs puts them in place of the deps' copies. A test
  without such a dep builds exactly as before. Only go_library deps can be
  built again: another rule's package that imports the package under test
  still conflicts with it (merge_pkgs).

The external test package is never coverage-instrumented, as with go test.

